ike to work which is it forces  you to think you know triple think  everything you're doing you know and go  through the script again triple think  all the decisions you're making because  I always find that that beautiful things  come out of that I'm reticent to call it  compromise because it isn't it's just  being rigorous in your interrogation of  the material and how you are planning to  execute it but then every now and then  something happens like you know they you  know we've got those that The Trevor  shows they're called you know and I  remember being in an early  pre-production meeting with the art  department they said so how many of  these do you want and I just said three  you know expecting someone to tell me at  some point later down the track that  you're gonna get half of one and we'll  see you the rest there was never another  conversation about I just turned up in  Hungary a few months later and there are  three of these [ __ ] things you know  there and they're amazing and we we shot  the [ __ ] out of them can you talk to me  about the physical challenges of putting  all this together you've invoked such an  interesting post medieval world you've  worked in multiple countries but what  were the challenges there I think for  this one it was a Zonk or budgetarily we  realized that we couldn't shoot it all  in the UK after we got that number and  so we had to find a rebate able place to  do the line share of the production and  then we had to send David there in  February when it was covered and so and  say definitely find your valley which he  did bless him  yeah I would I would say Agincourt for  all the obvious reasons the mud the heat  the horses the battle the armor but also  for the safety anxiety just a constant  prayer every day all day long let's all  get out of here okay  honestly because it was there was just  proximity was intense for a long period  of time and wanting these guys to stay  safe and happy and feel like they're  getting everything that they want and  also wanting to get out of there okay  and I want to thank you all for your  comments I think we're out of time

